			"widgets_values":[
				"【Narrative Intent】A cyan-robed cultivator standing on a broken stone bridge summons heavenly thunder with an ancient sword to cleave a towering tidal wave. Emotional goal: from suppressed tension to explosive release. Emotional arc: contrast-based.\n\n【Lighting Design】\nKey light: Backlit cool blue (7500K) + right-side warm golden side light (3200K) dual-key light opposition. Rim light: Silver-white edge light tracing along scapulae and blade edge. Contrast ratio: High (8:1). Atmospheric effects: Tyndall effect penetrating cloud layers + volumetric light pillars + instantaneous global high-brightness flashes during lightning strikes.\nColor palette: Teal & Orange cold-warm contrast. Dark areas lean toward cool jade-green, highlights lean toward warm amber, lightning strikes are blue-violet.\n\n【Sound Design】\nAmbient layer: Sustained howling wind + distant rumbling thunder + continuous roar of waves crashing against bridge foundations.\nFoley layer: Blade scraping metal friction upon drawing → high-frequency crackling explosion when lightning strikes → tearing whoosh of sword energy cleaving air.\nDialogue layer: No dialogue.\nEmotional layer: Heartbeat accelerates from 72bpm to 120bpm during power buildup; at the moment of release, heartbeat pauses for a half-beat followed by a single muffled bass drum hit.\nNon-narrative music: N/A (pure sound effect driven)\n\n【Visual Sequence】\n0-3 seconds — Medium full shot: The cyan-robed cultivator stands alone on the edge of the broken bridge ruins. Camera movement: Orbiting (4m radius, 25°/s) + slow ascent (2cm/s), rising from waist level to shoulder level. Action breakdown: Initiation — the cultivator's right ring finger presses the sword sheath mechanism, thumb braces against the guard, wrist rotates inward causing the sheath to tilt 2° leftward. Physical signals: Jawline tensed, Adam's apple slowly slides once, pupils locked onto the sea level horizon ahead. Environment: The lower hem of the cyan robe is blown 30° right-to-left by strong winds, fabric folds transmitting wave-like motion; right sleeve pressed tight against the forearm revealing muscle contours; floating water mist particles suspended in air are backlit into golden specks, rising and falling with breathing rhythm. Lighting: Tyndall light beams pierce through cloud gaps, illuminating bronze patterns on the sheath tip.\n\n3-6.5 seconds — Close-up: Sword-drawing initiation — left foot steps half-step backward crushing stone debris, the blade exiting the sheath brings out a trail of crackling electric sparks. Camera movement: Rapid push-in (15cm/s) from full shot to hand close-up + 0.3-second micro-rotation shake simulating energy resonance. Action breakdown: Process — thumb pushes the guard → blade exits one-third of the way as wrist flips upward → right arm extends while blade tip draws a clockwise arcing light trail → left palm gathers qi and strikes the sword guard producing a metallic resonance. Physical signals: Glabellar furrow deepens, masseter muscle tightens creating shadow depressions below cheekbones, dorsal veins bulge on the hand gripping the hilt. Environment: The moment electric sparks are triggered, blue-violet electrical arcs leap and jump 3 times from fissures beneath the feet; water droplets in the air instantly vaporize along the blade's trajectory forming a white mist arc; the left palm strike produces a ring of transparent shockwave ripples expanding outward. Lighting: Warm golden side light reflects a flowing amber luster across the blade surface; cool blue key light carves hard shadows on the left half of the cultivator's face; silver-white rim light flickers along the blade edge.\n\n6.5-8.5 seconds — Medium shot: Wave-cleaving strike — the cultivator lunges with a bow stance, twisting the waist to drive the blade diagonally downward from upper right to lower left. Camera movement: Low-angle upward shot (lens 1.2m below bridge level), rapid push-in (8cm/s) following the blade's downward trajectory, lens micro-shake as the blade enters frame. Action breakdown: Process — right shoulder pulls back for 0.4s power accumulation → hip rotation drives lumbar spine turning 15° → scapula powers the upper arm → elbow extension → wrist snap maximizes blade acceleration → blade edge cleaves into the center point of the towering wave crest. Recovery — left arm extends backward maintaining balance, right arm locks joints at the strike terminus, blade tip points 3° below the water surface. Physical signals: Neck veins protrude visibly, corner of the mouth twitches slightly, breath transitions from held suspension to a sharp explosive exhalation. Environment: The towering wave is split in two by sword energy, with both wave walls curling inward and churning; water droplets explode into thousands of translucent spheres splashing backward; gravel rolls off the broken bridge edge; the cyan robe is violently blown backward by the blast wave, hems flaring. Lighting: A blue-violet light ribbon appears along the sword energy's cutting path; water droplets in the spray exhibit starburst highlights against the backlight; the lightning flash momentarily shifts the entire scene's color temperature to cool white + blue-violet, then returns to the warm golden main tone.\n\n8.5-10 seconds — Full shot to extreme long shot: Residual force diffusion — the wave collapses to both sides, ripples expanding across the water surface. Camera movement: Pull-back (12cm/s) + ascent (6cm/s), pulling from full bridge view to a 40-meter aerial high-angle shot. Action breakdown: Recovery — the cultivator slowly straightens his waist, blade tip pointing three inches above the ground, left palm withdrawing from chest to dantian position, breath transitioning from rapid to prolonged and steady. Environment: The split wave transforms into drizzling rain falling upon the scene; residual electrical currents along the brick patterns fade; mist at the break point forms a faint rainbow within the final Tyndall beam. Lighting: Volumetric light re-condenses into soft golden beams through the rain curtain; cool blue key light transitions to a mixed gray-blue + warm gold; overall contrast lowers to medium-low. The scene freezes on the silhouette of the cultivator standing still on the broken bridge, facing away from the viewer.\n\nNot desired: No new characters appearing, no screen flashes, no facial distortion, no excessive CG plastic texture, no sudden cuts (one continuous shot throughout). Non-narrative music: N/A.",
